@startuml query_pipeline
title Authoritative event history query
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java d9a20777 plus commits through fa354fe2
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/CommittedEventQueryService.java#list
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java#findEventPage
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeSessionMapper.xml#countUnmappedCurrentBranchEntries
' Observed behavior: the production controller still uses the legacy history path.
' Design reason: switch HTTP only after every public writer uses atomic committed events.
' Java divergence: pi has no CampusClaw current-branch HTTP history store.
actor Caller
participant RuntimeEventController
participant CommittedEventQueryService
participant MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
database t_sessions
database t_session_entries
database t_session_event_projection
database t_session_events
participant CommittedEventProjection
participant ListSessionEventsResponseVO

Caller -> RuntimeEventController : GET page and limit (target switch pending)
RuntimeEventController -> CommittedEventQueryService : list(sessionId, limit, page)
CommittedEventQueryService -> MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository : findEventPage(offset, limit + 1)
activate MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository -> t_sessions : read session and active leaf
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository -> t_session_entries : resolve recursive current path
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository -> t_session_event_projection : verify exact completeness
alt unknown, missing, or partial mapping
  MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository --> CommittedEventQueryService : fail closed
else complete mapping
  MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository -> t_session_events : read stable order with offset and limit
  t_session_events --> MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository : committed event DTOs
  MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository --> CommittedEventQueryService : one page plus lookahead
end
deactivate MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
CommittedEventQueryService -> CommittedEventProjection : project each complete event
CommittedEventProjection --> CommittedEventQueryService : immutable public event VOs
CommittedEventQueryService -> ListSessionEventsResponseVO : events and nextPage
ListSessionEventsResponseVO --> Caller : JSON result

note over MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository,t_session_events
  One REPEATABLE_READ transaction per request.
  No cross-request snapshot or total count.
end note
@enduml

@startuml migration_flow
title Restart-safe legacy event migration
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java d9a20777 plus commit 749dc828
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/upgrade/V1_to_V2__schema.sql
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/upgrade/V1_to_V2__data.sql
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/upgrade/V1_to_V2__verify.sql
' Observed behavior: legacy entries lack enough safe data for a complete v2 projection.
' Design reason: exact reviewed mappings prevent Skill body and private thinking disclosure.
' Java divergence: this is a CampusClaw release migration, not a pi runtime behavior.
actor ReleaseOperator
participant SchemaScript
participant DataScript
participant VerifyScript
database t_session_entries
database t_session_sequences
database t_session_event_migration_review
database t_session_event_migration_events
database t_session_events
database t_session_event_projection

ReleaseOperator -> SchemaScript : run during maintenance window
SchemaScript -> t_session_events : create public authority
SchemaScript -> t_session_event_projection : create exact marker
SchemaScript -> t_session_event_migration_review : create release-only decisions
SchemaScript -> t_session_event_migration_events : create release-only events
ReleaseOperator -> t_session_event_migration_review : exact count and safe reason
ReleaseOperator -> t_session_event_migration_events : stable reviewed events
ReleaseOperator -> DataScript : run a bounded pass
DataScript -> t_session_entries : classify every legacy entry
DataScript -> t_session_event_migration_review : require unresolved decisions
DataScript -> t_session_event_migration_events : verify count, order, and references
alt complete session
  DataScript -> t_session_events : insert in stable legacy order
  DataScript -> t_session_event_projection : record exact completeness
  DataScript -> t_session_sequences : advance once
  DataScript -> t_session_event_migration_events : clear successful payloads
else gap or unknown type
  DataScript --> ReleaseOperator : leave session unchanged
end
ReleaseOperator -> VerifyScript : verify after each pass
VerifyScript -> t_session_entries : find missing or unknown mappings
VerifyScript -> t_session_events : verify counts and safe references
VerifyScript --> ReleaseOperator : IDs, types, fixed reasons only

note over DataScript,t_session_event_projection
  At most 500 complete sessions per pass.
  One session is committed as one atomic unit.
  A rerun never regenerates an event ID.
end note
@enduml
